{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And I will remember My covenant with Jacob.</b> In five places it is written full, and Elijah deficient in five places — Jacob took a letter from the name of Elijah as a pledge that he will come and proclaim the redemption of his children." "<b>And I will remember My covenant with Jacob.</b> Why are they counted in reverse order? That is to say: Jacob alone is worthy enough for this, and if he is not worthy enough, behold Isaac is with him, and if he is not worthy enough, behold Abraham is with him, who is worthy enough. And why was remembrance not stated for Isaac? Because the ashes of Isaac are seen before Me gathered and lying upon the altar (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:50.559106701Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}